@startuml
title Spec-Driven Development Flow (Mandatory vs Optional)

' ===============================
' Mandatory steps (default style)
' ===============================
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor Black
  FontColor Black
}

' ===============================
' Optional steps (visual distinction)
' ===============================
skinparam activity<<optional>> {
  BackgroundColor #F5F5F5
  BorderColor #888888
  BorderStyle dashed
  FontColor #444444
}

start

:Define Engineering Guardrails;
note right
Command:
/speckit.constitution

Purpose:
✔ quality standards
✔ testing expectations
✔ security & performance rules
✔ conventions & review norms

Artifact:
constitution.md
end note

:Define Requirements & Intent;
note right
Command:
/speckit.specify

Purpose:
✔ scope & objectives
✔ functional requirements
✔ success criteria
✔ constraints & assumptions

Artifact:
spec.md
end note

:Clarify & De-Risk Requirements; <<optional>>
note right
Command:
/speckit.clarify

Purpose:
✔ remove ambiguity
✔ define edge cases
✔ clarify NFRs
✔ specify data & API contracts
✔ align on acceptance tests

Artifact:
Updated spec.md
end note

:Design Technical Approach;
note right
Command:
/speckit.plan

Purpose:
✔ architecture & components
✔ data flows & interfaces
✔ tradeoffs & decisions
✔ risks & rollout approach

Artifact:
plan.md
end note

:Break Down Executable Work;
note right
Command:
/speckit.tasks

Purpose:
✔ ordered implementation steps
✔ dependencies & sequencing
✔ ownership & deliverables
✔ verification steps

Artifact:
tasks.md
end note

:Consistency & Governance Analysis; <<optional>>
note right
Command:
/speckit.analyze

Purpose:
✔ spec / plan / tasks alignment
✔ constitution compliance
✔ missing tests or constraints
✔ architectural gaps

Outcome:
✔ issues identified
✔ or ready to proceed
end note

if (Issues found?) then (Yes)
  :Refine Spec / Plan / Tasks;
  note right
  Purpose:
  ✔ address analysis findings
  ✔ re-clarify where needed
  ✔ update affected artifacts
  end note

  --> :Consistency & Governance Analysis;
else (No)
  :Readiness & Quality Checklist; <<optional>>
  note right
  Command:
  /speckit.checklist

  Pre-build gate:
  ✔ acceptance criteria complete
  ✔ test strategy defined
  ✔ security & privacy reviewed
  ✔ observability/logging planned
  ✔ rollback & failure modes considered
  end note
endif

if (Ready to build?) then (Yes)
  :Build & Test Solution;
  note right
  Command:
  /speckit.implement

  Purpose:
  ✔ execute tasks
  ✔ write code & tests
  ✔ follow constitution rules
  ✔ keep docs aligned
  end note

  :Validate & Deliver;
  stop
else (No)
  :Refine Spec / Plan / Tasks;
  note right
  Purpose:
  ✔ close checklist gaps
  ✔ update tasks or plan
  ✔ re-run gates as needed
  end note

  --> :Consistency & Governance Analysis;
endif

@enduml
